WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:02.570
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:02.570 --> 00:05.900
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:05.900 --> 00:08.390
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:08.390 --> 00:11.630
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:11.630 --> 00:14.120
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:14.440 --> 00:17.700
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:17.700 --> 00:23.630
But there was a girl who was fair and graceful, despite being in the middle of such battles.

00:23.630 --> 00:27.010
A fair and graceful girl? You, at the age of 23?

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:57.590 --> 01:58.530
Um...

01:59.340 --> 02:00.350
Yes?

02:00.700 --> 02:03.310
I'm trying to find something.

02:03.660 --> 02:06.310
What are you looking for?

02:06.310 --> 02:07.850
Something about book burning.

02:08.310 --> 02:09.150
Book burning?

02:09.600 --> 02:13.610
Information on the burning of books?

02:13.610 --> 02:14.290
Yes.

02:15.640 --> 02:17.120
Let me show you.

02:18.600 --> 02:21.040
That's a touchy subject in a library.

02:27.590 --> 02:32.040
Situation 07

02:27.590 --> 02:32.040
References on Love

02:33.200 --> 02:34.800
What's he like?

02:34.800 --> 02:36.460
His name is Asahina.

02:36.460 --> 02:40.390
She met him in the reference section, and then he asked her out.

02:44.870 --> 02:47.460
How old are you, if I may ask?

02:47.460 --> 02:49.540
I'm 23.

02:49.880 --> 02:52.330
You're two years younger than I am.

02:52.330 --> 02:54.070
I thought you might be a little older.

02:56.480 --> 02:59.490
I mean, with regards to your maturity, of course.

02:59.940 --> 03:02.050
You're so dependable.

03:02.740 --> 03:04.450
Thank you.

03:05.180 --> 03:08.020
She doesn't look very enthusiastic.

03:08.020 --> 03:08.920
No.

03:08.920 --> 03:10.790
She has her business face on.

03:14.870 --> 03:16.440
I'm sorry!

03:17.750 --> 03:18.760
Are you okay?

03:17.750 --> 03:18.760
I'm sorry!

03:20.340 --> 03:24.380
Am I bothering you by asking you out so many times?

03:24.380 --> 03:26.220
Not at all.

03:26.220 --> 03:29.750
I'm just assisting a patron.

03:29.750 --> 03:32.630
It seems that some of my colleagues are taking this the wrong way, though.

03:37.130 --> 03:40.390
That's because you're quite attractive.

03:40.390 --> 03:43.200
And by that, I mean how you look.

03:43.580 --> 03:45.040
Thank you.

03:45.560 --> 03:49.750
Is this research related to your everyday work?

03:50.100 --> 03:53.460
I'm doing some research on local governments.

03:53.460 --> 03:55.470
I've been working on issues regarding libraries recently.

03:56.130 --> 03:57.720
That's why you asked about book burning?

03:58.070 --> 03:59.190
Sorry about that.

03:59.190 --> 04:01.590
There's no need to apologize.

04:01.590 --> 04:06.770
Libraries have had a history of burning books to aid their country in its censorship.

04:07.520 --> 04:12.190
What do people from the Library think about that?

04:13.050 --> 04:15.180
And what about you personally?

04:17.350 --> 04:25.330
I think that it's good to observe the library system, while also acknowledging that it has made various mistakes in the past.

04:25.840 --> 04:30.140
It's never a good idea for any organization to mix public justice and individual justice.

04:30.560 --> 04:33.630
Are you talking about the Media Cleansing Committee?

04:34.780 --> 04:35.870
You think?

04:38.810 --> 04:41.450
May we talk again?

04:41.450 --> 04:44.570
I have no other friends who work at a library.

04:45.090 --> 04:51.570
I'm assisting you as a member of the Library staff, so I haven't thought of this as a friendship.

04:51.570 --> 04:52.740
Sorry.

04:53.690 --> 04:55.650
Well, in that case...

04:55.650 --> 04:58.020
Would you please accept this?

04:59.680 --> 05:02.930
It was rude of me to not offer you one yet.

05:03.860 --> 05:06.240
I can do nothing more than take it.

05:06.590 --> 05:09.040
Accepting it is all I ask of you.

05:09.040 --> 05:09.950
Well, for now.

05:11.520 --> 05:13.010
I'll take it.

05:14.940 --> 05:18.100
Oh man, she took it!

05:18.100 --> 05:20.010
A business card is nothing.

05:20.010 --> 05:21.090
No way!

05:21.090 --> 05:23.510
She wouldn't take it if she thought nothing of him!

05:23.510 --> 05:25.010
She wouldn't?

05:29.970 --> 05:34.930
I'll call you tonight,
be in your room.
- Satoshi

05:36.240 --> 05:38.290
How does he know my number?

05:39.570 --> 05:40.530
Who's it from?

05:41.840 --> 05:42.950
None of your business.

05:43.380 --> 05:47.070
Huh? What's with the attitude?

05:55.020 --> 05:56.920
I'm home.

05:57.320 --> 05:58.600
Welcome home!

05:58.600 --> 06:01.630
So, how was Asahina-san?

06:01.630 --> 06:04.840
Nothing special, really.

06:04.840 --> 06:09.350
Oh, come on, aren't you jumping up and down inside?

06:09.350 --> 06:11.650
You're the one...

06:13.370 --> 06:16.730
Oh, you were browsing that site?

06:18.350 --> 06:21.360
It's becoming a problem both inside and outside of the Library.

06:21.360 --> 06:24.610
It's very aggressive to be putting it on the Library's official page.

06:24.610 --> 06:27.530
And Sunagawa, our former classmate, is writing it.

06:27.530 --> 06:29.280
Who does he think he is?!

06:29.280 --> 06:33.470
He's bashing my favorite book, too!

06:33.470 --> 06:36.750
He's been changing lately.

06:36.750 --> 06:38.180
Really?

06:38.180 --> 06:42.720
I guess it started since he joined a group that researches problems with libraries.

06:42.720 --> 06:45.700
It's called the Future Library Project, I believe.

06:45.700 --> 06:49.220
Your network of informants is seriously scary.

06:50.940 --> 06:51.710
Yeah.

06:52.370 --> 06:55.180
All right, I'll come.

07:06.460 --> 07:07.530
Oh, hey.

07:08.060 --> 07:09.870
Oh, Sunagawa?

07:09.870 --> 07:11.580
These are hot items.

07:11.580 --> 07:13.080
Help me carry these.

07:13.080 --> 07:16.640
What's up with your scorching reviews?

07:18.180 --> 07:20.690
You'd better stop soon.

07:20.690 --> 07:22.630
All you do is bash the content of books.

07:22.630 --> 07:24.660
That's what people like.

07:24.660 --> 07:28.590
I'm sure there are patrons whose feelings have been hurt because their favorite books were bashed.

07:28.590 --> 07:32.970
There's a note included that says it's the personal opinion of a staff member.

07:32.970 --> 07:34.770
You don't have to read it if you don't like it.

07:35.200 --> 07:38.960
Don't you think it's inappropriate to put that on a public institution's site?

07:38.960 --> 07:41.320
Oh, come on, you too?

07:41.320 --> 07:44.400
The Library staff has freedom of expression too.

07:44.400 --> 07:46.440
Stop this quibbling!

07:46.440 --> 07:48.820
I don't approve of it.

07:48.820 --> 07:52.220
If you're still doing it the next time I see you, I'll strangle you to death for real.

07:54.490 --> 07:56.030
What an annoying girl.

07:56.030 --> 07:56.880
Later.

07:57.670 --> 08:01.450
Isn't Tezuka Satoshi your older brother?

08:05.590 --> 08:11.340
I joined the research group for the Future Library Project, the organization he's coordinating.

08:11.690 --> 08:15.910
It's a group that seriously considers censorship and society.

08:15.910 --> 08:18.440
He's the man!

08:18.440 --> 08:21.870
He can change this awful world.

08:21.870 --> 08:23.360
Stop it!

08:38.080 --> 08:39.380
Shibasaki-san!

08:41.680 --> 08:44.240
Is it possible to see Mount Fuji from this library?

08:44.970 --> 08:50.440
Well, if the weather is nice and the sky is clear, it can be possible.

08:50.440 --> 08:52.210
Where would I be able to see it?

08:53.060 --> 08:54.130
Do you know?

08:56.130 --> 08:57.430
I do.

08:58.010 --> 09:01.390
Could you take me there?

09:02.660 --> 09:04.890
Let me show you.

09:09.360 --> 09:10.800
Are you mad?

09:10.800 --> 09:11.730
No.

09:11.730 --> 09:12.840
Do you want to bet?

09:12.840 --> 09:14.000
If it's visible or not?

09:14.000 --> 09:14.960
Yes.

09:14.960 --> 09:16.460
No, thank you.

09:16.460 --> 09:17.990
It doesn't matter either way.

09:18.760 --> 09:20.200
Right.

09:25.140 --> 09:26.130
Here you go.

09:26.890 --> 09:27.780
Thank you.

09:30.400 --> 09:33.760
If I win, please let me take you out for dinner tomorrow evening.

09:34.570 --> 09:36.640
I'm not betting on it.

09:37.380 --> 09:39.560
I am just notifying you of the location.

09:40.940 --> 09:42.560
But aren't you curious?

09:44.450 --> 09:45.700
About whether we can see it or not?

09:48.790 --> 09:49.730
A little.

09:49.730 --> 09:51.900
In that case, I'll bet that it's visible.

09:52.860 --> 09:54.360
That's not fair!

10:08.180 --> 10:09.700
It's so pretty...

10:09.700 --> 10:11.370
I win.

10:11.370 --> 10:12.730
I never agreed...

10:30.080 --> 10:33.380
Isn't Tezuka Satoshi your older brother?

10:44.230 --> 10:46.930
You're an adult once you're in high school.

10:46.930 --> 10:49.320
You can carry around one of those things too.

10:51.380 --> 10:52.670
Thanks!

10:52.670 --> 10:55.380
I'll try not to trail too far behind you.

10:57.590 --> 11:00.300
That's wonderful, Hikaru.

11:07.440 --> 11:09.940
Aren't you being more careful than usual?

11:11.950 --> 11:13.900
It's the same as usual.

11:13.900 --> 11:17.770
Liar! You're doing two more things than usual!

11:17.770 --> 11:20.870
So you're a girl, too!

11:20.870 --> 11:22.450
That makes me, your mother, very happy.

11:22.450 --> 11:24.120
Don't mock me!

11:26.270 --> 11:29.380
So, are things moving along with Asahina-san?

11:29.950 --> 11:32.150
Did he ask you out for some tea tomorrow?

11:33.040 --> 11:36.090
Not tea.

11:36.090 --> 11:37.840
Then lunch, finally?

11:37.840 --> 11:39.140
Close.

11:39.140 --> 11:40.850
French.

11:40.850 --> 11:42.820
Dinner?!

11:42.820 --> 11:44.900
All done.

11:49.750 --> 11:51.770
Enjoy your date tomorrow.

11:52.370 --> 11:56.780
You have my full support if you're serious.

11:57.870 --> 11:58.660
Yeah.

12:00.330 --> 12:01.400
Good night.

12:14.310 --> 12:17.330
I didn't think that you'd agree to see me.

12:18.550 --> 12:20.120
It's because I owe you one.

12:21.910 --> 12:25.960
The actions taken by the Cleansing Force were clearly illegal that day.

12:26.310 --> 12:29.100
So the DoJ acted without us having to make much of a fuss.

12:35.390 --> 12:40.290
I heard that Sunagawa from our Operations Department is part of your research group.

12:40.810 --> 12:43.150
What's your motivation for drawing him in?

12:43.850 --> 12:46.090
Don't be so condescending about him.

12:46.090 --> 12:48.520
He's one of us, just like all the others.

12:48.520 --> 12:49.980
No matter how useless.

12:50.750 --> 12:52.280
Bullshit.

12:52.280 --> 12:54.190
You are different.

12:54.190 --> 12:57.990
Hikaru, won't you join my Future Library Project?

13:01.520 --> 13:05.970
Even after five years, all you can think about is taking advantage of me.

13:06.620 --> 13:08.890
You now know their internal workings.

13:08.890 --> 13:11.300
You're more useful than last time.

13:11.300 --> 13:13.500
I have no intention of cooperating with you.

13:14.430 --> 13:17.780
Hikaru, I'm sure you are starting to realize something.

13:17.780 --> 13:21.390
The Library Force is not an effective organization for fighting the censors.

13:21.390 --> 13:22.790
That's not true!

13:23.110 --> 13:28.310
Can you see a future without censorship when you fight with your guns?

13:28.310 --> 13:31.790
It's normal to fight as long as society is wrong, like it is now!

13:33.050 --> 13:34.800
We share a common belief.

13:34.800 --> 13:36.600
Censorship is unnecessary.

13:36.600 --> 13:39.590
Information should not be limited.

13:39.590 --> 13:42.730
However, appropriate controls are needed.

13:43.220 --> 13:45.620
And you want to do that?

13:45.620 --> 13:47.490
I'm sure it'll be fun.

13:52.560 --> 13:55.800
You betrayed and destroyed our family!

13:56.720 --> 13:59.730
Mom became sick because of you!

13:59.730 --> 14:02.310
And you never went to visit her after that!

14:02.820 --> 14:06.980
I couldn't help it, since I left home after having arguments with Dad.

14:06.980 --> 14:10.180
I can't believe that you can simply use that as an excuse!

14:11.210 --> 14:12.650
You're still green.

14:12.650 --> 14:15.860
I don't want a society controlled by you.

14:16.900 --> 14:18.110
Yeah?

14:19.600 --> 14:21.110
That's too bad.

14:22.220 --> 14:23.910
I'll retreat for now.

14:23.910 --> 14:26.170
But I haven't given up yet.

14:26.170 --> 14:28.370
I'll keep trying patiently.

14:48.330 --> 14:49.790
Delicious.

14:52.270 --> 14:53.450
Is something wrong?

14:54.670 --> 14:57.100
Shibasaki-san, I have something to tell you.

14:57.930 --> 15:00.390
I've been wondering for a long time, whether to tell you or not.

15:01.830 --> 15:06.720
It's information regarding the First Musashino Library.

15:07.050 --> 15:09.750
The source is a friend of mine who's a reporter.

15:10.320 --> 15:14.730
The First Musashino Library is disposing of books illegally.

15:14.730 --> 15:16.540
That's impossible.

15:16.540 --> 15:19.630
It would never happen so close to the Library Force.

15:19.630 --> 15:22.280
And why have I never heard of this?

15:22.280 --> 15:23.550
Right.

15:23.550 --> 15:26.170
So it's on a very small scale.

15:26.170 --> 15:27.900
So small that even you haven't heard of it.

15:28.330 --> 15:32.510
The reporter said that he'd report it as a case of modern book burning.

15:33.000 --> 15:37.640
But what would you do if I told you that we could still omit the story?

15:38.560 --> 15:42.390
He owes me enough that I could ask him not to report it.

15:48.230 --> 15:51.080
Why are you telling me?

15:52.000 --> 15:53.660
How long can we prevent it from leaking?

15:54.170 --> 15:55.550
Until the end of tomorrow.

15:55.550 --> 15:58.290
It'll go to the public if we don't stop him by then.

15:58.290 --> 15:59.340
It affects the entire library sys—

15:59.340 --> 16:00.470
I know!

16:01.370 --> 16:05.010
I'm sorry, but I can't give you my answer right now.

16:05.010 --> 16:07.280
I guarantee I'll give you the answer tomorrow.

16:07.280 --> 16:08.400
Let me go home tonight for now.

16:28.510 --> 16:30.840
But what would you do if I told you...

16:31.720 --> 16:32.860
that we could still omit the story?

16:37.310 --> 16:38.460
Welcome home.

16:39.650 --> 16:40.940
What's the matter?

16:40.940 --> 16:42.220
Nothing.

16:42.220 --> 16:43.830
It can't be nothing.

16:45.210 --> 16:47.180
Did something happen with Asahina-san?

16:50.870 --> 16:54.330
Kasahara, I want to ask you something.

16:55.570 --> 17:01.000
Imagine that someone you admire a lot was involved in a crime.

17:01.000 --> 17:02.910
Huh? What is this?

17:02.910 --> 17:04.050
What's this about?

17:04.050 --> 17:05.660
Just listen.

17:06.110 --> 17:11.270
What would you do if it were possible to completely conceal it before it was ever found out?

17:12.720 --> 17:14.460
That's not easy.

17:19.730 --> 17:21.210
I would...

17:23.170 --> 17:25.530
recommend him or her to surrender.

17:28.020 --> 17:33.380
Concealing a crime makes it impossible to make up for our mistakes.

17:34.300 --> 17:40.020
The punishment will be more severe if the subterfuge ever comes to light, too.

17:40.020 --> 17:41.460
Right...

17:41.460 --> 17:46.140
The Library staff I want to have around wouldn't forget about sins or mistakes.

17:46.990 --> 17:48.320
Thank you, Kasahara!

17:49.850 --> 17:53.210
This is why I love you so much.

17:56.920 --> 18:00.280
I'll pretend I never heard what you told me last night.

18:01.530 --> 18:02.640
You're sure?

18:03.340 --> 18:04.400
Yes.

18:04.400 --> 18:09.050
If this illegal disposal is true, we shouldn't keep it a secret.

18:09.580 --> 18:11.060
All right.

18:24.780 --> 18:26.200
This is Asahina.

18:26.200 --> 18:28.750
Just tell him that I'm from the DoJ.

18:29.810 --> 18:33.490
Hm, Hikaru's teammates are fastidious.

18:33.490 --> 18:36.420
This wasn't the only hook or bait out there, though.

18:36.420 --> 18:40.730
But for now, let's have them enjoy the news that will come out tomorrow.

18:47.180 --> 18:51.310
After an internal investigation which was triggered by a report from an outside party, the curator of this library, Eto,

18:51.310 --> 18:58.620
has announced that illegal disposal of books by some of the staff at the First Musashino Library has occurred.

19:03.360 --> 19:06.490
Captain Genda, you were aware of this?

19:06.490 --> 19:10.740
Wasn't that announcement made without the proper protocol of the Library?

19:10.740 --> 19:13.140
They even outsmarted you, eh.

19:13.140 --> 19:18.150
I heard that there was a report made to Commander Inamine before the announcement.

19:18.150 --> 19:20.490
It's still just grandstanding!

19:22.070 --> 19:24.530
That's not the only problem we have.

19:25.120 --> 19:30.150
This hasn't been made public yet, but Sunagawa from Operations is involved in this case.

19:32.130 --> 19:33.590
Sunagawa is?

19:33.590 --> 19:36.770
You mean Sunagawa was performing the illegal disposals?

19:38.850 --> 19:40.710
Dojo, come with me.

19:49.650 --> 19:51.000
That's impossible!

19:51.000 --> 19:53.520
Please take back that order!

19:53.520 --> 19:54.790
Calm down!

20:02.080 --> 20:03.080
Kasahara,

20:05.130 --> 20:09.420
The Interrogation Commission has ordered you to report to them.

20:13.790 --> 20:17.720
Sunagawa named you as an accomplice.

20:22.700 --> 20:25.420
You look calm, Kasahara-san.

20:25.860 --> 20:26.910
Yes.

20:27.850 --> 20:32.280
Because it sounds like someone got upset in my stead.

20:35.410 --> 20:38.800
But I heard that their interrogation is really tough.

20:39.980 --> 20:41.980
Like how?

20:41.980 --> 20:44.880
How tough was it, Dojo?

20:45.480 --> 20:47.020
How would I know?

20:47.020 --> 20:51.890
There was someone from this group who was ripped to shreds by the Interrogation Commission, too.

20:52.950 --> 20:55.970
Sir? Is something wrong?

20:55.970 --> 20:57.190
Nothing at all.

20:57.190 --> 20:59.520
That's not a face that says no...

20:59.520 --> 21:05.900
How can I stay calm when my idiot subordinate is summoned to their interrogation?

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
Goodbye my old self

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
ushinau mono mo aru

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
There are things I'll lose too

